}\cdots x_{k_{q}}\right)  \right)   &  =\left\langle \left.  \Phi_{f}\left(
x_{j_{1}}\cdots x_{j_{p}}\right)  \right\vert \Phi_{f}\left(  x_{k_{1}}\cdots
x_{k_{q}}\right)  \right\rangle _{\mathcal{H}_{f}}\\
0  &  \leq j_{1}<\cdots<j_{p}\leq2r,0\leq k_{1}<\cdots<k_{p}\leq2r;0\leq
p,q\leq2r.
